                "reviews": [
                    {
                        "recommendationid": "37167545",
                        "author": {
                            "steamid": "76561198005338092",
                            "num_reviews": 27,
                            "playtime_forever": 7958,
                            "playtime_last_two_weeks": 0,
                            "playtime_at_review": 7778,
                            "last_played": 1532641471
                        },
                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "At this point of Galactology is good fun for 10-30 hour \"session\", after which endgame content starts to run out. But don't worry about that going to the game, you'll enjoy it before that happens. It's quite free from bugs and plays really well from begining to the moment you decide to quit. Updates come regularly and add nicely to the gameplay. Developer is active and communicative about plans for the game. \n\nSo, Galactology is essentially a base builder with fun comic graphics. It's easy to get into and understand the mechanics, interface is first a little old fashioned feeling, but is actually very user friendly. Tutorial is a bit simple/annoying, but you can just ignore it if you have played these games before. Economics simulation is what you can expect, you always make profit, but you can optimise quite a fair amount. If you quickly build stuff that you just reasearched you run into shortages, also at early midgame you can easily run out of money, but pile up tons soon after. Unfortunately there isn't much use for money, so once it starts to pile you don't need to save it for anything. \n\nPlanet exploration is all about harvesting materials from new planets. It's essential part to the game. It's part of the game mechanics that at this point doesn't offer much - you pop bulding's and leave, but isn't especially boring either and there is decent amount of visual variation. Materials are carried back to the base by your autopiloted ships. There is kind of fun aspect of invasions on planets you are harvesting from, so from time to time you have to go fight and liberate the planet guns blazing.\n\nGalactology might be the best light base builder at the moment. To be a gem it would need more humor (now it's just \"funny\" graphics), little bit improved economics system and some special thing to make it really \"unique\". It might might be able to pull it off if future updates keep coming. But as it is, it's already great.\n\n4/5 stars. Review updated after release from EA.",
